{"name":"Almond Butter","hex":"#d8c6a8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almond butter","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of food paste made from almonds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almond_butter"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almond butter","blocks":[{"text":"Almond butter is a food paste made from grinding almonds into a nut butter. Almond butter may be \"crunchy\" or \"smooth\", and is generally \"stir\" or \"no-stir\" (emulsified). Almond butter may be either raw or roasted, but this describes the almonds themselves, prior to grinding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Breville_Boss-_Almond_Butter_%28square_crop%29.jpg/330px-Breville_Boss-_Almond_Butter_%28square_crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almond_butter","wikidata":"Q4733896"},{"title":"Almond","blocks":[{"text":"The almond is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/330px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almond","wikidata":"Q15545507"},{"title":"Butter","blocks":[{"text":"Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream. It is a semi-solid emulsion at room temperature, consisting of approximately 81% butterfat. It is used at room temperature as a spread, melted as a condiment, and used as a fat in baking, sauce-making, pan frying, and other cooking procedures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-%C5%A0v%C3%A9dsk%C3%BD_kol%C3%A1%C4%8D_naruby_904_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter","wikidata":"Q34172"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors","wikidata":"Q6568034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ametllesjuliol.jpg/500px-Ametllesjuliol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ametllesjuliol.jpg/1280px-Ametllesjuliol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ametllesjuliol.jpg/500px-Ametllesjuliol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmetllesjuliol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85_%D9%88_%D8%B4%DA%A9%D9%88%D9%81%D9%87_%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85.JPG/250px-%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85_%D9%88_%D8%B4%DA%A9%D9%88%D9%81%D9%87_%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%AF%D8%A7%D9%85.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, htt